= Collective action — Technical =

Collective-action problems are often modeled with social dilemmas such as n-person prisoner's dilemmas, threshold public-good games, or common-pool resource games. The equilibrium structure depends on contribution costs, benefit functions, monitoring, repeated interaction, sanctioning, and institutional rules.

== Modeling cautions ==
* collective action ≠ coordination problem
* collective action ≠ cooperation only
* free-rider problem ≠ every collective-action problem

== References ==
* Mancur Olson, ''The Logic of Collective Action'' (1965).
* Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, “The Free Rider Problem” (current revision).
* Elinor Ostrom, ''Governing the Commons'' (1990).
